  ('meribel-france', '01F', 'Méribel', 'France', 'The wooded heart of the world''s biggest ski area', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'French Alps', '{"ski","family","romance","ultra","hiking","wellness","culinary"}', '{"alpine","refined","family-friendly"}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["Geographic heart of Les 3 Vallees — world''s largest linked ski area: 600 km slopes + 50 km ski routes, 159 lifts, 1,100-3,230 m, 7 linked resorts","Meribel valley: ~150 km pistes, 76 runs (8 green/36 blue/23 red/9 black), 53 lifts; villages Les Allues 1,100 m to Mottaret 1,750 m; top Mont du Vallon 2,952 m","Central pivot — ski to Courchevel (via La Saulire) AND Val Thorens/Belleville (via Mont de la Chambre) and home the same day; 85% of domain above 1,800 m","Founded by Scot Major Peter Lindsay from 1938 with a wood/stone/slate chalet-only building code — the catered-chalet capital and British-favourite family/apres base","Racing pedigree: 1992 Albertville Olympics (men''s ice hockey + women''s Alpine); 2023 FIS Alpine World Ski Championships women''s races on the Roc de Fer","Luxury layer: Le Coucou (5-star, 55 keys + 2 chalets, ski-in/ski-out at 1,600 m) and L''Helios (5-star, 18 keys + spa)","Domain scale: 340 marked runs, 105 km2 skiable, 53 high-altitude restaurants, 2,700 snow guns; 3V slope mix 336 km easy / 204 km intermediate / 60 km difficult","Best time Dec-Apr (Feb most snow-sure, Mar best conditions); green summer Jun-Sep ~20 C for hiking + biking"],"safety":{"emergency":"112 (EU all-services) / 15 SAMU medical / 17 police / 18 fire; mountain rescue via PGHM (dial 112)","hospital":"In-resort medical centres (Meribel Centre + Mottaret); regional Centre Hospitalier Albertville-Moutiers (CHAM), Moutiers site ~18 km; serious trauma transfer Grenoble/Chambery, often by helicopter","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"High-alpine winter sports: off-piste avalanche risk (Meteo-France Meribel bulletin, European 5-level scale; transceiver/shovel/probe + guide), cold/altitude, glacier terrain guided-only; PGHM via 112","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/france","read":"2026-08-20T14:48:26Z","page_updated":"2026-08-11T10:17:02+01:00","source_country":"france","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely"},"timing":{"peak":"High winter — Christmas/New Year + February half-terms (British + French); highest chalet/hotel rates, min-stays, Sat changeover congestion","shoulder":"Early Dec (pre-Christmas value) + late-season Mar-Apr spring-ski (sun, long days, lower rates)","green":"May-Jun + Oct-Nov (lifts/chalets closed); Jul-Aug modest summer programme (hiking/biking) at lowest rates","booking_lead":"Christmas/NY + Feb half-terms 4-9 mo (best chalets + five-stars, min-stay); regular winter 2-4 mo; spring/summer 1-2 mo","off_season_specials":"Spring-ski value (late Mar-Apr); summer 3 Vallees hiking/biking (Jul-Aug); shoulder wellness short-breaks","event_peaks":"Christmas/NY, February half-terms, Easter spring-ski; event weeks tied to World Cup/championship legacy (verify calendar)","fire_date":"Next winter + peak catered chalets by Jun-Aug (long chalet lead + min-stays); spring-ski from Jan; summer 3 Vallees from spring"},"jewels":[{"name":"Ski the entire 3 Vallees from the doorstep — 600 km on one pass","si_tag":"Winter/Ski","status":"live","tier":"comfort","price_band":"~EUR 75-95/day lift (approx; verify)","timing":"ski ~early Dec-late Apr; verify","draw_rank":1,"hook":"Méribel is the only base from which you can reach Courchevel, Val Thorens and the Belleville valley in a single day on skis","si":"ski","blurb":"Méribel is the only base from which you can reach Courchevel, Val Thorens and the Belleville valley in a single day on skis","when":"ski ~early Dec-late Apr; verify","commission":"school/operator 10-15%","wells"